; ted-prtfile-ascii-tokens (#371): Print takes every byte >= $80 and the
; byte behind it for a token, also without tokenising: a Latin-1
; character and the next one are printed as a bold token name.  TED alone
; (no token list: tokenise off; under blitz2 TED tokenises, and tokit
; clears bit 7 of the text), lines "; Größe", "b"; PRINT into the file
; TEDRUN:work/prt.txt, QUIT.  Correct: the lines as they are; the original
; prints "; Gr", ESC[1m, the "name" findtoke finds without a token list
; ("?????" when the long word at address 0 is 0), ESC[22m, "e".
; @file bo.bas "; Gr\xf6\xdfe\nb"
; @source F bo.bas
; @command blitz2:ted @FILE@
; @expect data prt.txt "; Gr\xf6\xdfe\nb\n"
timeout 10
wait screen
menu 0 5
wait req "PRINT" "CANCEL"
str 1 "TEDRUN:work/prt.txt"
gad 2
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
